<title>USA: LG&amp;E says had losses on 'rogue' trading.</title>
<headline>LG&amp;E says had losses on 'rogue' trading.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>LG&amp;E Energy Corp said Friday natural gas marketing unit LG&amp;E Natural Inc discovered a &quot;rogue&quot; marketer in its Calgary, office.</p>
<p>It said the marketer made unauthorized and fraudulent transactions which resulted in significant losses in the company's Canadian natgas marketing business.</p>
<p>LG&amp;E Energy said its 1996 earnings will exceed that of 1995, but the &quot;rogue&quot; trading will probably cause it to fall short of anticipated year-end earnings.</p>
<p>The First Call consensus estimate for LG&amp;E for the full year is $1.59 per share, up from 1995's $1.53.</p>
</text>
